From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Fri, 07 Aug 2026 16:15:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: guard op_class update in CSA fallback

ieee80211_freq_to_channel_ext() leaves *op_class untouched on every
failure path, and hostapd_switch_channel_fallback() declares it
uninitialized, so the unconditional assignment could store a garbage
stack byte into conf->op_class. That value then feeds
configured_fixed_chan_to_freq() and the op_class_to_ch_width() width
override during the interface restart. Assign only when the
conversion succeeds, matching the guarded idiom the DFS code already
uses, and keep the previous op_class otherwise.

Vendor patch 0057-era companion 0074 does not address this: it adds
a second, guarded write after the garbage one, and its recompute
reads the operating width after the ieee80211ac/ax/be flags were
already overwritten, which goes stale across an ieee80211be
transition. It was rejected in favor of this fix.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 src/ap/hostapd.c |   15 +++++++++------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -5057,12 +5057,15 @@ hostapd_switch_channel_fallback(struct h
 	if (ieee80211_freq_to_channel_ext(freq_params->freq,
 					  freq_params->sec_channel_offset, bw,
 					  &op_class, &chan) ==
-	    NUM_HOSTAPD_MODES ||
-	    chan != freq_params->channel)
-		wpa_printf(MSG_INFO, "CSA: Channel mismatch: %d -> %d",
-			   freq_params->channel, chan);
-
-	iface->conf->op_class = op_class;
+	    NUM_HOSTAPD_MODES) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_INFO, "CSA: No op_class for freq %d, keeping %d",
+			   freq_params->freq, iface->conf->op_class);
+	} else {
+		if (chan != freq_params->channel)
+			wpa_printf(MSG_INFO, "CSA: Channel mismatch: %d -> %d",
+				   freq_params->channel, chan);
+		iface->conf->op_class = op_class;
+	}
 	hostapd_set_oper_centr_freq_seg0_idx(iface->conf, seg0_idx);
 	hostapd_set_oper_centr_freq_seg1_idx(iface->conf, seg1_idx);
 	hostapd_set_oper_chwidth(iface->conf, bw);
